<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>💧 LIVE WATER QUALITY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/bacteria/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Human-health concern from fecal-indicator evidence, FIXED log scale (E.coli-equiv CFU/100 mL): <b>DARK BLUE 10</b> (no detected/lowest) &rarr; <b>BLUE 30</b> (very low) &rarr; <b>CYAN 60</b> (low) &rarr; <b>LIGHT GREEN 100</b> (low-to-moderate) &rarr; <b>DARK GREEN 126</b> (moderate, EPA GM) &rarr; <b>YELLOWISH GREEN 190</b> (elevated) &rarr; <b>YELLOW 235</b> (concerning, EPA Beach Action Value) &rarr; <b>ORANGE 320</b> (high) &rarr; <b>RED 410</b> (very high, EPA STV) &rarr; <b>NEON RED 700</b> (extremely high) &rarr; <b>MAGENTA 1000</b> (severe) &rarr; <b>PURPLE 2000</b> (extremely severe) &rarr; <b>DARK PURPLE HIGHEST+ 5000+</b> (extreme). <b>LOWEST 10</b>. Water without observations stays transparent (<b>NO DATA</b>, slate swatch in key) — never zero bacteria.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: USGS Water Quality Portal (WQX E. coli / enterococci / fecal coliform) + EPA BEACON beach-advisory framework + EPA 2012 RWQC & 1976 Red Book thresholds).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>💧 LIVE WATER QUALITY — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Water_Quality.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>3600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
